    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0327" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.01/518a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>)<anchor n="25" xml:id="d272-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-15T19:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>513. You will have seen from Buenos Aires telegram no. 1494, June 12,<anchor
                        n="26" xml:id="d272-f2"/> that official Argentine release quotes texts of
                    notes exchanged <pb facs="0328" n="314" xml:id="pg314"/> between Ecuadoran
                    Foreign Office and Argentine Ambassador in Quito thus confirming the conclusion
                    in your no. 602, June 13,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d272-f3"/> that Ecuador is
                    extending full recognition to the Farrell government. It is difficult for us to
                    comprehend how this could have occurred after jour conversation with Foreign
                    Minister reported in your no. 561, June 3, 1 p.m.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d272-f4"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>Please arrange to see Foreign Minister at once and point out serious implications
                    of position apparently adopted by Ecuador directly contrary to non-recognition
                    policy being followed by 17 other American Governments.</p>
                <p>In view of official statement released in Buenos Aires please advise the Foreign
                    Minister that some official clarification by Ecuadoran Government seems called
                    for immediately. Such a clarification might take the form of an announcement
                    that the Ecuadoran government does not intend to make a decision with regard to
                    the appointment of an Ambassador to Argentina or with regard to carrying on
                    normal diplomatic relations with the Farrell regime until it has had an
                    opportunity for full consultation with the other American Republics.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
